From 9971943d22d1e5a26571efec4b86a253831ed512 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:47:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: match package metadata to the Unleashed executable
 version

Use the numeric vendor build or dev suffix in the default package version.
Expose the same version through a query command so downstream packaging can
retain its license and archive handling without duplicating version policy.
Explicit package-version overrides remain available.

Base: rust-v0.160.0 (a956835d020762cb2b570053af06f643a11c0ecc).
Runtime companion: add-branding-and-build-metadata.patch.

TDD: CODEX_REPO_ROOT="$PWD" python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/codex_package -p test_cli.py
failed on the unpatched base: expected +41 and +dev, received bare 0.160.0.
Green: CODEX_REPO_ROOT="$PWD" python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/codex_package -p 'test_*.py'
31 tests passed, including the package CLI defaults, explicit override and
version-query command. The downstream production entry point built a package
from a real 0.160.0+41 executable and recorded version 0.160.0+41.
