 The `--variant` flag selects the package entrypoint. Supported variants are
 `codex` and `codex-app-server`. The `--package-version` flag sets the version in
-`codex-package.json`; it defaults to `[workspace.package].version` in
-`codex-rs/Cargo.toml`.
+`codex-package.json`. The default combines `[workspace.package].version` in
+`codex-rs/Cargo.toml` with
+`+<CODEX_UNLEASHED_BUILD_NUMBER>`, matching the Unleashed executable. Without
+that environment variable, source-built packages use `+dev`. When packaging
+prebuilt executables, supply the build number used to compile them. An explicit
+`--package-version` overrides this default.
 
 ## Source-built artifacts
 
